"Tropicana Corporation Berhad (Registration no:197901003695 (47908-K)) (https://www.tropicanacorp.com.my/pdf/TCB%20-%20Minutes%20of%20the%2046th%20AGM.docx%20%28Final%29.pdf)\nciteturn327search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.2 years ago; Minutes of the 46th Annual General Meeting held on 25 June 2025 ... <td>Tropicana Cenang, Langkawi<br>– Clarissa Serviced Suites and Beachwalk Shoppes (806 units)</td> ... (1) Edelweiss Serviced Residences and SOFO, Tropicana Gardens, Tropicana Indah\nTropicana Corporation Berhad (Registration no:197901003695 (47908-K))  \nMinutes of the 46th Annual General Meeting held on 25 June 2025\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>FY2024<br>RM’ million</th>\n<th>FY2023<br>RM’ million</th>\n<th>%<br>Change</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Total equity and liabilities</b></td>\n<td><b>10,485.5</b></td>\n<td><b>11,978.6</b></td>\n<td><b>(12.5%)</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total cash (RM)</td>\n<td>696.4</td>\n<td>500.5</td>\n<td><b>39.1%</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gross gearing (times)</td>\n<td>0.43</td>\n<td>0.54</td>\n<td><b>(20.4%)</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Net gearing (times)</td>\n<td>0.30</td>\n<td>0.46</td>\n<td><b>(34.8%)</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total no. of shares in issue (million)</td>\n<td>2,467.0</td>\n<td>2,266.3</td>\n<td><b>8.9%</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Net assets/share (RM)</td>\n<td>1.67</td>\n<td>1.90</td>\n<td><b>(12.1%)</b></td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n(c) Summary of Upcoming Developments\n\n<table id=\"e2\">\n<tr>\n<th>Project name</th>\n<th>Gross development value (RM)</th>\n<th>Target launch date</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Lido Waterfront Boulevard, Johor<br>– Skypark Kepler Branded Residences (1,596 units)</td>\n<td>1.6 billion</td>\n<td>Quarter 2 2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tropicana Cenang, Langkawi<br>– Clarissa Serviced Suites and Beachwalk Shoppes (806 units)</td>\n<td>1.01 billion</td>\n<td>Quarter 2 2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tropicana Avalon, Genting Highlands<br>– Breeze Hill Shoppes and Service Apartments (1,722 units)</td>\n<td>1.2 billion</td>\n<td>Quarter 3 2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tropicana Danga Bay, Johor<br>– Bora Residences (245 units)</td>\n<td>199 million</td>\n<td>Quarter 3 2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tropicana Paradise, Genting Highlands<br>– Serviced Suites (798 units)<br>–</td>\n<td>646 million</td>\n<td>Quarter 4 2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tropicana Paradise, Genting Highlands<br>– Bungalow Lots (39 units)</td>\n<td>127 million</td>\n<td>Quarter 4 2025</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tropicana Uplands, Gelang Patah<br>– Fraser Heights Terrace Homes (295 units)</td>\n<td>225 million</td>\n<td>Quarter 3 2025</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n(d) Market Traction and Future Growth\n\nTropicana remains committed to monitoring key performance metrics, maintaining cost-efficiency measures, and launching new developments aligned with market demand. As an experienced master planner and developer, the Group remains agile and responsive to evolving market trends and customer preferences.\n\nDevelopments with Full Take-up Rates in FY2024\n\nThe Group achieved 100% take-up rates for the following developments during FY2024:  \n(1) Edelweiss Serviced Residences and SOFO, Tropicana Gardens, Tropicana Indah  \n(2) Gemala Residences, Tropicana Aman, Kota Kemuning  \n(3) Tropicana Miyu, Petaling Jaya  \n(4) Freesia Residences, Tropicana Aman, Kota Kemuning\n\n3--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTropicana Corporation Berhad (https://www.tropicanacorp.com.my/magazine-detail/327)\nciteturn327search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; As this integrated development enters its final phase, anticipation is building for the Edelweiss Serviced Residences, SOFO, and Shoppes, set to be completed by 2025. ... Limited to 38 units, these commercial shoppes span two floors, with unit sizes ranging from 250 sq ft to 2,433 sq ft, thoughtfully designed to cater to diverse commercial needs.\n\nTrump Card\n\nTrump Card\n\nImage: Trump Card - Detail\n\n##### Tropicana Gardens, the hallmark development by Tropicana Corporation Berhad, has recently earned the prestigious title of the best mixed-use development in Malaysia at the FIABCI Malaysia Property Award 2023. As this integrated development enters its final phase, anticipation is building for the Edelweiss Serviced Residences, SOFO, and Shoppes, set to be completed by 2025.\n\n##### \nTropicana Gardens stands out as an exceptional development, featuring five Green Building Index (GBI) Certified Residential Towers, a sprawling 1 million sq ft Tropicana Gardens Mall, and an Office Tower, all seamlessly connected to the Surian MRT station. Positioned as the vibrant heart of Tropicana Indah and celebrated as one of Malaysia's top Transit-Oriented Developments (TOD), Tropicana Gardens has proven to be a valuable investment, offering positive rental yields and convenient amenities to the affluent neighborhood.\n\nImage: Trump Card - Detail\n\n##### The final phase, named Edelweiss, is emerging within a robust ecosystem where residents can live, work, play, shop, and learn, all while enjoying seamless connectivity through the Surian MRT station. This walkability factor not only promotes a healthy lifestyle but also helps reduce our carbon footprint.\n\n##### \nTropicana Gardens is part of the sustainable 405-acre Tropicana Indah township, which began its journey in 1996. Over the past 28 years, it has evolved into one of the most sought-after addresses in Petaling Jaya, fulfilling Tropicana's grand vision of creating a sustainable, livable, and prosperous township with excellent connectivity. This aligns with Tropicana’s mission to \"Redefine the Art of Living,\" focusing on well-connected townships with timeless designs and extensive amenities.\n\nImage: Trump Card - Detail\n\n##### Your Last Chance to Own a Piece of Tropicana Gardens\nSince its inception, Tropicana Gardens has seen tremendous success. The first residential tower, Arnica, launched in 2012, sold out in just two days, followed by Bayberry, Cyperus, and Dianthus Serviced Residences, which also achieved 100% take-up. In 2020, Tropicana Gardens Mall and Tropicana Office Tower opened their doors to high occupancy rates.\n\n##### \nThe final phase, the Edelweiss Serviced Residences, SOFO, and Shoppes, valued at RM855 million, are currently under construction and will be completed by 2025. Launched in October 2020, the Edelweiss Serviced Residences and SOFO have already recorded a healthy 90% take-up. Recently launched, the Edelweiss Shoppes represent the last commercial opportunity in this mature neighborhood.\n\nImage: Trump Card - Detail\n\n##### Strategically connected to major highways such as NKVE, LDP, DASH, Penchala Link, and Sprint Highway, the Edelweiss Shoppes offer an ideal business address for entrepreneurs looking to relocate or expand their retail offerings. Limited to 38 units, these commercial shoppes span two floors, with unit sizes ranging from 250 sq ft to 2,433 sq ft, thoughtfully designed to cater to diverse commercial needs.\n\n##### \nKey Features of Edelweiss Shoppes\n•    Shopping Mall Proximity: Enjoy maximum convenience next to a 1.1 million sq ft shopping mall.\n•    Integrated Development: Seamlessly connected with the Serviced Residences and SOFO.\n•    GreenRE Certification: Targeting a Silver GreenRE rating with eco-friendly fixtures.\n•    Ready Catchment: Benefit from foot traffic from Tropicana Gardens Mall, Surian MRT station, and Seri Selangor Golf Club.\n•    Direct MRT Connection: Easy access via a covered link bridge to the Surian MRT station.\n•    Self-Sustainable: Strong internal traffic flow supported by residents and SOFO occupants.\n•    High Visibility: Most units are highly visible from the main road, ensuring high traffic.\n•    Unique Offering: The only fully covered, air-conditioned commercial area within a 15km radius.\n\n##### \nJoin this exclusive community and become part of a dynamic lifestyle. Secure your spot today and discover more about Edelweiss Tropicana Gardens at https://edelweiss.tropicanagardens.com.my. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROSSSPERITY AWAITSSS with Tropicana! (https://campaign.tropicanacorp.com.my/AoSCNY2025/)\nciteturn327search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; ### 1^{st} Jan - 28^{th} Feb 2025 ... Limited Units Available ... ## Tropicana Gardens - Edelweiss Serviced Residences\n\n# PROSSSPERITY AWAITSSS\nwith Tropicana!\n\n## Start the prosperous New Year with our exclusive deals and incredible Prosperity Packets.\nSecuring your very own dream home has never been easier !\n\n### 1^{st} Jan - 28^{th} Feb 2025\n\nMore Info\n\niframe\n\nImage Image\n\nLegal Fees &\nStamp Duty Absorbed\nby Developer*\n\nFurnishing Package\nWorth Up To RM60k*\n\nFlexible Financing\nSolutions*\n\nExciting\nReferral Rewards*\n\n*Terms & Conditions apply.\n\n# Let us know\nYour preferred region\n\n[Button: Klang Valley ] [Button: Other Regions]\n\nImage\n\nLegal Fees & Stamp Duties Subsidy\n\n## Tropicana Aman - 2, 3 & 4 Storey Shop Offices\n\nInvest in Elite Shop Offices\n\n* * *\n\nImageKota Kemuning\nImage2, 3 & 4 Storey Shop Offices\n\n* * *\n\nPrice From RM1.8 Mil\n\nView Brochure View Flyer\n\nImage\n\nLimited Units Available\n\n## Tropicana Metropark - SouthPlace Shoppes\n\nYour New Hangout Spot at Subang Jaya\n\n* * *\n\nImageSubang Jaya\nImageRetail Lots\n\n* * *\n\nPrice From RM1.2 Mil\n\nView Brochure View Flyer\n\nImage\n\nExclusive Furnishing Package\n\n## Tropicana Metropark - SouthPlace 2 Residences\n\nAn All-New Living Experience\n\n* * *\n\nImageSubang Jaya\nImageServiced Residences\n\n* * *\n\nPrice From RM660K\n\nView Brochure\n\nImage\n\nLegal Fees & Stamp Duty Subsidy\n\n## Tropicana Metropark - SouthPlace 2 Shoppes\n\nYour New Hangout Spot at Subang Jaya\n\n* * *\n\nImageSubang Jaya\nImageRetail Lots\n\n* * *\n\nPrice From RM1.2 Mil\n\nView Broch